<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heinrich von Zütphen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1488">1488</a>–<a href="/years/1524">1524</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Henry of Zutphen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heinrich von Zütphen (1488–1524) was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Augustinian friar and follower of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a>. Having escaped imprisonment in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, he began preaching in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a> in 1522 and won the city for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>. In 1524 he went to preach in Dithmarschen, where he was seized by a mob and burned, becoming one of the first martyrs of the Lutheran Reformation.</p></div>
